config CAN_AGRV2K
	bool "AgRV2K CAN (SJA1000-compatible PeliCAN) driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_AGM_AGRV2K_CAN_ENABLED
	select CAN_SJA1000
	select PINCTRL
	help
	  Enable support for the on-die CAN controller on AgRV2K SoCs.
	  The IP is register-compatible with the NXP SJA1000 in
	  PeliCAN mode; this driver is a thin frontend that plugs into
	  the shared can_sja1000.c state machine.

	  End-to-end verification goes through the controller's
	  MOD_SELFTEST (self-test) mode, exposed as CAN_MODE_LOOPBACK
	  through the upstream Zephyr CAN API — but it still needs a bus
	  the controller reads as idle: with nothing attached to the CAN
	  pins the transmitter never starts (SR.TS stuck, no error
	  counters). Keep the transceiver/peer on the
	  pins, as on the dev board. See samples/can_loopback/.
